      "writtenOn": "2026-03-03T18:45:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also need to be documented how this scan works.\n\nLet\u0027s assume:\n\nVMA: 0x100000 - 0x300000 but pages are mapped only 0x200000 - 0x300000\n\nIn this context, if user pass start_addr 0x200000 and request_bytes 0x100000, then end_addr will be 0x200000 or 0x300000?\n\nI think we should do latter 0x300000 because what we want to do is not queuing too much IO for writeback to preempt it with prefetch and here, the page table scanning is pretty cheap compared to the IO.\n\n\nFor the naming, how about just saying \"size\" likewise other syscalls?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "556b79c909bae0ce3e41ecb5c13301e95ca0f226",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
