    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc3a013e_427c146b",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/zram_ioctl.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275554
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-04T23:46:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For UAPI, pages is troublesome since they need to be aware of which PAGE_SIZE host system they are running on.",
      "parentUuid": "a4de4e60_8b6860d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "556b79c909bae0ce3e41ecb5c13301e95ca0f226",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "861ab64e_b8da10eb",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/zram_ioctl.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 3489357
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T03:28:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, my concern is that zram works with PAGE_SIZE units, and usually it\u0027s that conversion from bytes to num-pages etc. where we can have unexpected results (or even bugs).\n\nBut... considering writeback limit, which is in 4K units (unfortunately), I wonder if we have to align interfaces and use that same 4K granularity, just for consistency.",
      "parentUuid": "cc3a013e_427c146b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "556b79c909bae0ce3e41ecb5c13301e95ca0f226",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b88a76cc_37d336cd",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/zram_ioctl.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1894539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T15:04:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, I prefered bytes for userspace, more easy to understand than 4K units.",
      "parentUuid": "861ab64e_b8da10eb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
